S['filter-open']['instruction']='Lift the fuel-cap cover from its rear as shown, using both hands. Loosen the aircase-cover quick fastener; release both side ribs from scoop projections and slide the cover forward. Turn the two retaining plates in the diagram direction. Withdraw the air-filter guide and separate foam element, inner guide and seal without admitting dirt into the intake.'
S['filter-close']['instruction']='Fit seal and inner guide into the foam, then fit the foam to the air-filter guide. Grease the entire seal lips with lithium-soap grease. Engage both rear guide projections in the case slots and verify a continuous seal with no trapped, turned-up foam or gap. Rotate both retaining plates back. Engage the cover rear slots over case edges and align its side ribs with scoop projections; secure the quick fastener and restore breather routing. Restore the fuel-cap cover with its plastic bands fully beneath the seat.'
S['oil-drain']['instruction']='Upright on level ground, warm the engine several minutes, stop and wait about five minutes. Place a clean container under the single drain. Remove filler cap and drain bolt with gasket; drain the oil. Inspect for dirt and foreign material, especially metal chips. If present, stop: Yamaha requires crankcase disassembly and inspection before proceeding.'
S['filter-renew']['instruction']='Renew the oil filter during this oil change. Remove cover and old filter. Apply lithium-soap-based grease to the new cover O-ring from diagram234, install it, and fit the exact new filter in diagram90 orientation. Refit cover bolts10Nm. Filter renewal is included in this route; the post-break-in list itself requires the oil change.'
S['generator-access']['instruction']='With oil drained, first remove the fuel-cap cover because its plastic band couples it to the seat. Remove the left side cover, seat, aircase cover and left air scoop. Label and disconnect stator and crank-position couplers. Remove shift pedal, preserving punch-mark alignment. Record the lead holders retained with the left-cover hardware; keep the engine installed.'
S['generator-open']['instruction']='Release cover fasteners progressively and lift the cover without pulling wires. Retain both dowels and external lead holders; discard the gasket. Keep stator, internal holder and sealed grommet attached to the cover and rotor attached to the shaft. Secure assemblies do not require removal merely for a mounting inspection.'
S['generator-close']['instruction']='Fit both dowels and a new left-cover gasket. Restore the cover and external lead holders in diagram225 and tighten cover bolts in stages and crisscross to10Nm. Preserve undisturbed grommet sealing and unpinched wires. Align pedal/shaft punch marks and tighten pedal bolt12Nm; reconnect both couplers and restore illustrated lead routing.'
S['oil-fill']['instruction']='Fit a new gasket and tighten the single drain bolt20Nm. Fill0.65L for this filter-removal service. Use Yamalube or oil meeting API SG or higher and JASO MA; listed SAE grades are10W-40,10W-50,15W-40,20W-40 or20W-50 selected for ambient conditions. Do not add chemical additives or admit dirt. Check retained filler cap and seal condition before installing. Record actual oil/product. The0.90L disassembled-engine capacity is not this service refill; flow and exact final level checks remain required.'
S['oil-level']['instruction']='With bike upright on level ground, warm for2–3minutes, stop and wait about1minute. Check that oil is above the window minimum mark. Remove the oil-check bolt: oil must not flow out; if it does, drain excess until the last drop stops. Add specified oil if at/below minimum. Restore the bolt and its seal using verified exact closure information and record actual fastening and leak-free closure; no nearby cover torque is a substitute. Both window and check-bolt criteria must pass.'
S['oil-level']['verification']='Record2–3minute warm-up, approximately1minute wait, above-minimum window, no excess from check opening, and actual verified oil-check-bolt/seal closure. Stop completion if exact closure remains unresolved.'
